{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final operator-approved AC6 rewrite/review attempted. Plan-review still returned BLOCK, so per instruction I am leaving this ticket open and unclaimed; no Terraform apply, mount, Docker restart, or code work was performed. Blocking finding verbatim: AC6/§5 requires emitting a metric from assert_volumes_in_service.py's three-value classification (IN_SERVICE / NOT-IN-SERVICE / UNKNOWN) into the observability path, but never defines the emitted metric's value vocabulary nor how the three enum members map onto it — leaving the distinctness the script deliberately preserves (UNKNOWN != NOT-IN-SERVICE) at risk of being silently collapsed by a binary heartbeat. Checklist item: Define AC6's emitted-metric value vocabulary: name the metric, and specify the exact numeric value each classification (IN_SERVICE / NOT-IN-SERVICE / UNKNOWN) emits, explicitly preserving UNKNOWN as distinct from NOT-IN-SERVICE and stating the alarm threshold semantics for each."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788785434819242001,"uuid":"45d5b364-a407-4e65-9257-7664ae5faaa4"}